WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.448
In Europe, Amazon operates in five marketplaces, including the United Kingdom, Germany, France,

00:00:12.448 --> 00:00:15.320
Italy, and Spain.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.449
If you are currently selling in the U.

00:00:18.449 --> 00:00:18.810
S.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:21.698
marketplace, selling in Europe with linked accounts and

00:00:21.698 --> 00:00:26.392
build international listings tool simplifies the listing process and gives you the opportunity

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:28.920
to leverage Amazon's fulfillment network in Europe.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.861
After your North American account and Europe account are linked.

00:00:32.861 --> 00:00:34.472
You can select the U.

00:00:34.472 --> 00:00:34.794
S.

00:00:34.794 --> 00:00:39.303
as your source marketplace and add your offers to any of the five European

00:00:39.303 --> 00:00:41.880
target marketplaces by using build international listings tool.

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:47.264
In order to take advantage of FBA programs in Europe, you need to ship your inventory

00:00:47.264 --> 00:00:48.108
from the U.

00:00:48.108 --> 00:00:48.390
S.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:50.360
to an Amazon fulfillment center in Europe.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:55.900
Also, your product needs to meet the rules, regulations, and laws of each European country.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:01.427
For example, value added tax, also called VAT, in the European Union, is a consumption

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:05.040
tax assessed on the value added to your products and services.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:09.824
It applies to products and services that are bought and sold for use or consumption in

00:01:09.824 --> 00:01:10.620
the European Union.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:14.520
The European consumers don't see a separate line item for tax.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:20.930
Amazon's solution provider network, SPN, connects you with more than 100 high quality

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:26.238
solution providers who offer services such as shipping, VAT, product compliance, translation,

00:01:26.238 --> 00:01:26.680
etc.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.416
For more information, you can visit Amazon.

00:01:30.416 --> 00:01:31.700
com/SPN.

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:37.415
After your products are delivered to an Amazon fulfillment center in Europe, you can fulfill

00:01:37.415 --> 00:01:40.340
your orders across Europe through three international fulfillment programs.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:45.573
In this video, you'll learn about the three international FBA services in Europe, which

00:01:45.573 --> 00:01:48.140
make cross-border sales much easier to manage.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:55.660
These three programs are Pan-European FBA, European fulfillment network, and multi-country inventory.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:02:00.397
By enrolling in one of these programs, you're eligible for prime benefits, which gives you

00:02:00.397 --> 00:02:03.460
the ability to ship products to customers with free standard shipping.

00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:07.780
Now, let's take a look at the first program, Pan-European FBA.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:12.860
Pan-European FBA is the ultimate in European sales solution.

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:18.446
With it, Amazon places your inventory at close proximity to your customers, providing faster

00:02:18.446 --> 00:02:20.600
delivery, and growing your business quicker.

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:26.798
The Pan-European FBA program allows you to ship your inventory to one location, and Amazon

00:02:26.798 --> 00:02:31.378
will distribute your inventory across the European fulfillment network based on anticipated customer

00:02:31.378 --> 00:02:33.140
demand at no additional cost.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:37.655
When a customer orders your products, you only pay local fulfillment fee of the marketplace

00:02:37.655 --> 00:02:39.160
where the order is placed.

00:02:39.740 --> 00:02:46.065
To use Pan-European FBA, simply enroll your eligible ASINs in the Pan-European FBA inventory

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:46.460
page.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:53.015
You will be able to enroll eligible ASINs after you create an FBA offer in each of the Amazon

00:02:53.015 --> 00:02:54.940
European marketplaces from the same inventory.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:03:00.764
Activate ASIN auto-enrollment and Amazon will enroll eligible ASINs for you as soon as you

00:03:00.764 --> 00:03:02.040
create the FBA offers.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:07.260
To learn more, go to Seller Central in Europe and search Pan-European FBA in help.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:12.909
The European fulfillment network, or EFN, is a good choice if you're just getting started

00:03:12.909 --> 00:03:14.240
with selling in Europe.

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:20.000
EFN is a simple way to ship your inventory across all five of Amazon's European marketplaces.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:21.340
Here's how it works.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:27.056
First, you list the products in one or more of the Amazon European marketplaces with the

00:03:27.056 --> 00:03:28.340
Build International listings tool.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:32.400
Next, you ship your inventory to one of the fulfillment centers in Europe.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:37.642
Then, customers across Europe can order your products, and Amazon fulfills those orders

00:03:37.642 --> 00:03:39.420
from your Amazon inventory location.

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:44.507
When customers track their orders, they can see where they are shipping from, and the

00:03:44.507 --> 00:03:45.480
expected arrival time.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:50.702
For example, if you've shipped your products to a fulfillment center in the UK and a customer

00:03:50.702 --> 00:03:52.853
in Germany purchases your product on Amazon.

00:03:52.853 --> 00:03:56.200
de, the product is fulfilled by Amazon and shipped

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:59.400
from your inventory in that UK fulfillment center to Germany.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:05.281
You pay UK to Germany cross-border fulfillment fee in addition to the Germany local FBA fulfillment

00:04:05.281 --> 00:04:05.600
fee.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:11.600
To learn more about EFN, sign in to Seller Central in Europe and search EFN in help.

00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:17.940
So, what are the differences between Pan-European FBA and European Fulfillment Network?

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:23.971
First, Pan-European FBA requires selling in all five European marketplaces, while EFN

00:04:23.971 --> 00:04:26.820
lets you choose up to five marketplaces.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:33.712
Second, with Pan-European FBA, Amazon manages your inventory placement at no cost and moves

00:04:33.712 --> 00:04:37.520
it across the Amazon European Fulfillment Network based on customer demand.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:42.232
EFN, on the other hand, Amazon won't move your inventory out of the country where you

00:04:42.232 --> 00:04:43.280
shipped your products to.

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:48.947
Finally, you only pay the local FBA fee with Pan-European, while there is an additional

00:04:48.947 --> 00:04:50.840
cross-border fulfillment fee with EFN.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:56.817
If you're not ready to sell to all marketplaces in Europe through Pan-European FBA and don't

00:04:56.817 --> 00:05:02.156
want to pay the cross-border fulfillment fee through EFN, you can use the Multi-Country

00:05:02.156 --> 00:05:03.660
Inventory, or MCI, program.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:08.649
With MCI, you send your inventory directly to countries in Europe where customers are

00:05:08.649 --> 00:05:11.380
buying, so your customers will receive your products quickly.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:17.780
The differences between Pan-European FBA and Multi-Country Inventory are as follows.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:23.889
First, Pan-European FBA requires selling in all five marketplaces, while you can choose

00:05:23.889 --> 00:05:26.180
up to five EU marketplaces with MCI.

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:32.441
Second, with the Pan-European FBA service, you ship products to a single country, then

00:05:32.441 --> 00:05:37.400
Amazon moves your inventory across the Amazon European Fulfillment Network at no cost.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:42.400
With MCI services, you ship your products to Amazon in each country yourself.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:48.874
Last, with the Pan-European FBA service, Amazon manages your inventory and moves it across

00:05:48.874 --> 00:05:51.920
the Amazon European Fulfillment Network based on customer demand.

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:56.742
With the Multi-Country Inventory service, you have to identify how much inventory to

00:05:56.742 --> 00:06:01.380
send to each country, and your inventory is stored only in the country you ship to.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:03.480
That's all for this video.

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:08.180
Now you should have a good understanding of the three FBA international services in Europe.

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:14.005
If you want to learn more about the Fulfillment by Amazon services in Europe, go to services.

00:06:14.005 --> 00:06:14.507
amazon.

00:06:14.507 --> 00:06:15.009
co.

00:06:15.009 --> 00:06:15.511
uk

00:06:15.511 --> 00:06:18.020
and choose Fulfillment by Amazon.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.820
To get started, click Sell globally below.

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:22.160
Happy selling!
